※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1 run=native,qemu exit=0 diag=none

※ A sum made on one turn of a loop and kept for the next.
※
※ The room a sum is made in is the frame's, one for each place in the program a
※ sum is made at, so the next turn makes its value in the same room.  A name that
※ may change and holds such a value has storage of its own, and giving it a
※ value copies the bytes in: what it was given on one turn is still what it
※ holds on the next, whatever the next made in the room the value came from.
type Shape = line : u32 | empty : void

let std := ⎕import("std")

fn size(s: Shape) → u32:
    match s:
        u32(n):
            n
        void:
            0u32

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let prev: mut Shape = Shape(.empty ← true)
    let seen: mut u32 = 0u32
    foreach i := 1u32…4u32:
        let cur: Shape = Shape(.line ← i)
        seen ← seen × 10u32 + size(prev)
        prev ← cur
    if seen = 12u32: 0u6 else: 1u6
